CHECK:BIT_MACRO: Prefer using the BIT macro
#50: FILE: fs/nfsd/netns.h:29:
+#define CLIENT_HASH_SIZE                (1 << CLIENT_HASH_BITS)

Defines like: 1 << <digit> could be BIT(digit).
The BIT() macro is defined via include/linux/bits.h::

  #define BIT(nr)         (1UL << (nr))

CHECK:LINE_SPACING: Please don't use multiple blank lines
#162: FILE: fs/nfsd/nfs4recover.c:418:
 
+

Vertical space is wasted given the limited number of lines an
editor window can display when multiple blank lines are used.

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#spaces

CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kmalloc(sizeof(*nn->reclaim_str_hashtbl)...) over kmalloc(sizeof(struct list_head)...)
#169: FILE: fs/nfsd/nfs4recover.c:425:
+	nn->reclaim_str_hashtbl = kmalloc(sizeof(struct list_head) *

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

